  },
  "riscvGuidanceCrossCompilerLinux": "Install your distribution's package (gcc-riscv64-unknown-elf on Debian and Ubuntu, riscv64-elf-gcc on Fedora and Arch), or unpack an xPack or SiFive prebuilt. Set riscv.toolchain.path if it lives off PATH.",
  "@riscvGuidanceCrossCompilerLinux": {
    "description": "Remediation for a missing RISC-V cross-compiler on Linux."
  },
  "riscvGuidanceCrossCompilerMacos": "Install it with brew tap riscv-software-src/riscv, then brew install riscv-gnu-toolchain. An app launched from Finder does not inherit your shell's PATH, so a Homebrew install can be invisible — relaunch SimCrux from a terminal or set riscv.toolchain.path.",
  "@riscvGuidanceCrossCompilerMacos": {
    "description": "Remediation for a missing RISC-V cross-compiler on macOS."
  },
  "riscvGuidanceCrossCompilerWindows": "Windows is the least well-trodden path for this toolchain. xPack prebuilts do work, but riscv-arch-test's linker scripts and target plugins assume a POSIX layout, so running the whole flow under WSL2 is the better-supported option.",
  "@riscvGuidanceCrossCompilerWindows": {
    "description": "Remediation for a missing RISC-V cross-compiler on Windows."
  },
  "riscvGuidanceReferenceModelLinux": "Build Sail from riscv/sail-riscv, or install Spike (riscv-isa-sim), which is the easier of the two. Set riscv.reference.path to the binary, or switch riscv.reference.model.",
  "@riscvGuidanceReferenceModelLinux": {
    "description": "Remediation for a missing reference model on Linux."
  },
  "riscvGuidanceReferenceModelMacos": "Install Spike with brew tap riscv-software-src/riscv, then brew install riscv-isa-sim. Sail builds on macOS but takes effort. Remember that a Finder launch does not inherit your shell's PATH.",
  "@riscvGuidanceReferenceModelMacos": {
    "description": "Remediation for a missing reference model on macOS."
  },
  "riscvGuidanceReferenceModelWindows": "Sail has no practical native Windows build, and SimCrux will not pretend otherwise by spawning a command that cannot work. Run the flow under WSL2, or switch riscv.reference.model to spike, which the OSS CAD Suite ships for Windows.",
  "@riscvGuidanceReferenceModelWindows": {
    "description": "Remediation for a missing reference model on Windows, where Sail has no practical native build."
  },
  "riscvGuidanceRiscofLinux": "Install it into a virtualenv: python3 -m venv .venv, activate it, then pip install riscof. Activate that venv before launching SimCrux, or point riscv.riscof.command at .venv/bin/riscof.",
  "@riscvGuidanceRiscofLinux": {
    "description": "Remediation for a missing RISCOF on Linux."
  },
  "riscvGuidanceRiscofMacos": "Install it into a virtualenv: python3 -m venv .venv, activate it, then pip install riscof. Activate that venv before launching SimCrux, or point riscv.riscof.command at .venv/bin/riscof.",
  "@riscvGuidanceRiscofMacos": {
    "description": "Remediation for a missing RISCOF on macOS."
  },
  "riscvGuidanceRiscofWindows": "RISCOF installs cleanly on Windows and is the one component of the four that gives no trouble here: py -m venv .venv, activate it, then pip install riscof. Point riscv.riscof.command at the venv's riscof.exe if SimCrux was launched outside it.",
  "@riscvGuidanceRiscofWindows": {
    "description": "Remediation for a missing RISCOF on Windows."
  },
  "riscvGuidanceFormalEngineLinux": "Install the OSS CAD Suite bundle — it ships Yosys, SymbiYosys and the SMT solvers together.",
  "@riscvGuidanceFormalEngineLinux": {
    "description": "Remediation for a missing SymbiYosys on Linux."
  },
  "riscvGuidanceFormalEngineMacos": "Install the OSS CAD Suite bundle, or Yosys with Homebrew plus SymbiYosys from source. A Finder launch does not inherit your shell's PATH.",
  "@riscvGuidanceFormalEngineMacos": {
    "description": "Remediation for a missing SymbiYosys on macOS."
  },
  "riscvGuidanceFormalEngineWindows": "The OSS CAD Suite ships a Windows build; running it under WSL2 is also common.",
  "@riscvGuidanceFormalEngineWindows": {
    "description": "Remediation for a missing SymbiYosys on Windows."
  },
